Notebook[{
Cell["Traffic Flow Dynamics in the Wolfram Language", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"d6cd0dfc-fc91-4b0e-b24d-82aba8e40644"],

Cell["\<\
From phantom jams on a ring road to a full-city multi-agent simulation of \
Aberdeen \[LongDash] a self-contained port of classical traffic-flow models.\
\>", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"eca1002c-4590-4fd9-9b06-91a38af318e8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Marco Thiel, April 2026 \[LongDash] ",
 ButtonBox["github.com/mthiel74/TrafficJAms",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://github.com/mthiel74/TrafficJAms"], None}]
}], "Text",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontSlant->Italic,ExpressionUUID->"63da0b97-b1c6-4ceb-a3e9-9d212daddd68"],

Cell["Abstract", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"62425ca3-49f3-422e-b486-80581df3bcdb"],

Cell["\<\
Traffic jams are the canonical everyday example of an emergent phenomenon: \
each driver follows simple local rules, and the system as a whole \
spontaneously produces stop-and-go waves, phantom jams, shockwaves, and \
city-scale gridlock. Since the 1950s these have been modelled at wildly \
different scales \[LongDash] as a hyperbolic PDE (Lighthill\[Dash]Whitham\
\[Dash]Richards), as individual vehicles following an ODE (Intelligent Driver \
Model, Bando OVM), as a stochastic cellular automaton \
(Nagel\[Dash]Schreckenberg), as a queueing network at intersections, or as a \
convex optimisation problem on a directed graph (Wardrop equilibrium). This \
notebook walks through all of those in turn, each with a short derivation, a \
Wolfram-Language implementation, and output from a real simulation. The \
running case study is Aberdeen in north-east Scotland \[LongDash] a city \
whose peculiar geography (squeezed between the Rivers Don and Dee, the coast, \
and the hills, with two critical bridges) makes it an unusually nice \
traffic-engineering laboratory. The final section applies the full pipeline \
to the 11\\[ThinSpace]925-node Aberdeen drivable road network extracted from \
OpenStreetMap, with 600 agents, UK-standard 90\[ThinSpace]s signal cycles, \
and roundabout gap acceptance.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8cdb05e8-8562-4b58-8fe8-aa4825006bcc"],

