    {
     PaneBox[
      StyleBox["\<\"Figure 5. Animated Bando OVM on an 800 m ring with 40 \
vehicles, seeded by a 5 m position perturbation on one vehicle. The ring \
starts in near-uniform flow; the perturbation rotates around the ring, grows \
via the Hopf instability, and breaks the symmetry into a persistent \
stop-and-go wave. The mean-speed readout in the centre collapses from ~13 m/s \
to under 1 m/s as the instability saturates. (MP4: \
Wolfram/results/anim_bando.mp4.)\"\>",
       StripOnInput->False,
       FontFamily->"Helvetica",
       FontSize->10,
       FontSlant->Italic],
      Alignment->Center,
      ImageSize->520]}
   },
   DefaultBaseStyle->"Column",
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Center}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{0.6}}}],
  "Column"]], "Output",
 CellMargins->{{20, 20}, {10, 14}},
 ShowCellLabel->False,
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"a36af9db-359d-4e03-a83c-279410b48dd4"],

Cell["6. A stochastic cellular automaton: Nagel-Schreckenberg", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c4560335-0233-49af-80af-1ce192d2acf4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Nagel and Schreckenberg (1992) gave the minimal CA that reproduces \
realistic traffic dynamics. Space is discretised into 7.5\[ThinSpace]m cells, \
time into 1\[ThinSpace]s steps, and velocity is an integer in [0, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["v", "max"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "5c52df02-d036-4365-9417-8cad6babef68"],
 "]. At each step every vehicle applies four rules:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3d5d631b-a3a2-4738-9fa0-e0d686b7fc47"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{"(", "1", ")", " ", 
   RowBox[{"accelerate", ":"}], " ", "v", "\[Rule]", 
   RowBox[{"min", "(", 
    RowBox[{"v", "+", "1"}], ",", " ", 
    SubscriptBox["v", "max"], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"f7991786-5107-4fa8-823a-6b827109180c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{"(", "2", ")", " ", 
   RowBox[{"brake", ":"}], " ", "v", "\[Rule]", 
   RowBox[{"min", "(", "v", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"d", "-", "1"}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"a76f4df9-dfaf-4853-9928-6cb850c9d3d7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{"(", "3", ")", " ", 
   RowBox[{"randomise", ":"}], " ", 
   RowBox[{"with", " ", "probability", " ", "p"}], ",", " ", "v", "\[Rule]", 
   RowBox[{"max", "(", 
    RowBox[{"v", "-", "1"}], ",", " ", "0", ")"}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"92534b6c-4d69-453d-9c0b-0ec863e9354c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{"(", "4", ")", " ", 
   RowBox[{"move", ":"}], " ", "x", "\[Rule]", 
   RowBox[{"x", "+", "v"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"d455d639-a6c8-432c-b00d-a447ec2ee6b2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["d", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "4b6b4268-426d-4213-8fba-90cd7e0c8eb8"],
 " is the number of empty cells to the next vehicle. The stochastic slow-down \
rule (3) is essential: without it the model reduces to a deterministic CA and \
does not jam spontaneously. With it, the space-time diagram spontaneously \
generates backward-propagating \"wave\" bands, matching the LWR and IDM \
results from a completely different starting point."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"962616ea-49d1-42fd-8fcc-ad3936643547"],

