    {
     PaneBox[
      StyleBox["\<\"Figure 9. M/D/1 queueing on a four-intersection corridor. \
Top: per-intersection queue length (left) and waiting time (right) as a \
function of utilisation; both blow up as rho -> 1. Bottom: total queue and \
total delay for a 4-intersection tandem. The red dashed line marks the \
rho=0.85 severe-congestion onset.\"\>",
       StripOnInput->False,
       FontFamily->"Helvetica",
       FontSize->10,
       FontSlant->Italic],
      Alignment->Center,
      ImageSize->520]}
   },
   DefaultBaseStyle->"Column",
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Center}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{0.6}}}],
  "Column"]], "Output",
 CellMargins->{{20, 20}, {10, 14}},
 ShowCellLabel->False,
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"3803205c-2766-4bc5-a919-59a1d5bdaaeb"],

Cell["8. Optimising the signal timing", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"fb177137-7660-46a0-9d05-d7f641555693"],

Cell["\<\
Given a corridor of signals at which arrivals vary by intersection, what \
green times minimise total delay, subject to a shared green-time budget? \
Delay at each intersection combines the M/D/1 waiting term above with \
Webster's uniform delay for the fraction of the cycle spent red,\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"00e412c0-f436-456f-8d1f-6c1d424b78bc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"d", 
    SubscriptBox["", "unif"]}], "=", 
   FractionBox[
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "C", "-", "g", ")"}], "2"], 
    RowBox[{"2", "C"}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"934e0836-0cba-4a49-ae2f-679a3f2e3023"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["C", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "969ba337-ef54-4c32-975c-88e9a70d723a"],
 " is cycle length and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["g", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "aec95175-2462-463e-a9ba-7dd6ab89ede4"],
 " is green time at the intersection. Minimising the sum of these over green \
times subject to a total budget is a smooth convex problem and ",
 StyleBox["FindMinimum[..., Method -> \"InteriorPoint\"]", "Input"],
 " solves it in milliseconds. On a five-intersection Union Street-like \
corridor with arrival rates (0.08, 0.15, 0.22, 0.17, 0.06), the optimum \
re-allocates green from the two quiet intersections to the central busy one \
and cuts total delay by ~8.4 %."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"59eef61f-f2a8-46c7-b989-911338488c65"],

